@startuml
title Victim Selection - After Strategy Pattern
caption Implemented design - Deadlock Playground

left to right direction

skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontSize 13
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundcorner 0
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam ArrowColor #444444

skinparam class {
  BackgroundColor #FFFFFF
  BorderColor #444444
  FontColor #222222
}

class SimulationEngine <<Facade>> {
  + recover(...)
}

interface VictimPolicy {
  + selectVictim(...)
}

class PriorityPolicy {
  + selectVictim(...)
}

class ResourcesHeldPolicy {
  + selectVictim(...)
}

class RecoveryCostPolicy {
  + selectVictim(...)
}

class Process {
  - id: String
  - priority: int
}

SimulationEngine ..> VictimPolicy : selects and uses

VictimPolicy <|.. PriorityPolicy

VictimPolicy <|.. ResourcesHeldPolicy

VictimPolicy <|.. RecoveryCostPolicy

VictimPolicy ..> Process : evaluates eligible victims

note top of VictimPolicy
  Strategy interface.

  Defines a common contract
  for selecting a recovery victim
  from eligible processes.

  Recovery Cost is the
  default policy.
end note

note bottom of PriorityPolicy
  Selects the eligible process
  with the lowest priority.
end note

note bottom of ResourcesHeldPolicy
  Selects the eligible process
  holding the fewest
  resource units.
end note

note bottom of RecoveryCostPolicy
  Selects the eligible process
  minimizing:

  Resources Held
  + Instructions Executed
end note

note right of Process
  Selection uses the current
  process state and metrics.

  Ties are resolved using
  the lower process ID.
end note

legend bottom
  AFTER STRATEGY PATTERN

  Implemented abstractions:
  VictimPolicy
  PriorityPolicy
  ResourcesHeldPolicy
  RecoveryCostPolicy

  SimulationEngine delegates
  victim selection to a policy.

  New selection algorithms can
  implement the same interface.

  Policy registration or mapping
  may still require updates.

  Method signatures are simplified
  for conceptual UML readability.

  Terminate and Preempt are separate
  recovery strategies and are not
  detailed in this diagram.
endlegend

@enduml
